Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:34:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 053/143] config: regenerate opi4a_blindboot_defconfig from the
 validated .config

The defconfig had drifted from the .config actually built and tested on
the board: later config changes had touched the local .config but not
the versioned defconfig, which is what gets published and what anyone
rebuilding from the README uses. Kernels built from it ended up with
RESET_GPIO=m (which breaks the AP6256 WiFi through mmc-pwrseq-simple),
watchdog and DRM as modules, no IOMMU, no HDMI console, and without the
analog codec, PCIe, the VPU, joydev or uinput.

Regenerated with 'make savedefconfig' from the validated .config; the
round trip (defconfig -> .config) gives zero differences.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
